.TH APKM 1 "2026-10-05" "apkm 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
apkm \- signed Android APK repository client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B apkm
[global-options] command [arguments]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Download verified APK files from configured HTTPS repositories and invoke
apkg to install them on an authorized Android target.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B source add NAME URL --keyring PATH
Verify and add a repository using a previously trusted binary GPG keyring.
.TP
.B source add NAME URL --type fdroid [--keyring PATH]
Add a GPG-signed F-Droid v1 repository. The official f-droid.org/repo
uses the bundled official key; other repositories require --keyring.
Stable variants are selected by Android API and ABI.
.TP
.B source list | source remove NAME
List or remove configured repositories.
.TP
.B update [SOURCE ...]
Download and verify signed indexes; omit sources to refresh all.
Search, info, install and upgrade use the local verified cache.
Legacy 0.2.0 caches are reused; missing caches require update.
.TP
.B source set-url NAME URL
Verify a mirror index using the existing trusted key and rollback checks,
then replace the source URL while retaining the source name.
.TP
.B search KEYWORD | info NAME
Search or inspect repository applications.
.TP
.B install [--download-only] [--output-dir PATH] NAME ...
Download, verify and optionally install single APK files.
.TP
.B upgrade [NAME ...]
Upgrade installed applications recognized by the configured repositories.
.TP
.B list | doctor
List Android applications or diagnose the backend.
.TP
.B remove PACKAGE-ID ...
Uninstall after confirmation. Package IDs are Android package names.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Place global options before the command.
.TP
.B --mode auto|adb|root
Prefer authorized ADB in auto mode; otherwise verify local Android host root.
.TP
.B --serial SERIAL
Select an ADB device. Required when multiple devices are connected.
.TP
.B --json
Emit newline-delimited JSON events.
.TP
.B --no-progress
Disable intermediate download progress events.
.TP
.B --yes
Skip uninstall confirmation, not Android authorization.
.TP
.B --version | --help
Show version or help. Subcommands accept --help.
.SH FILES
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/apkm/sources.json
or ~/.config/apkm/sources.json contains repository URLs and trusted keyring paths.
.PP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/apkm/apks/
or ~/.cache/apkm/apks/ stores verified downloads.
.SH SECURITY
Repository signatures and APK hashes are verified before installation.
Do not trust a public key solely because it arrived from the same untrusted site.
APK update signing compatibility is enforced by Android.
Linux root and PRoot simulated root do not imply Android host root access.
.SH PROGRESS
Download events contain actual byte counts. Android installation generally
provides status and completion rather than continuous percentages.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 general or partial failure; 2 invalid usage/configuration;
3 backend/authorization failure; 4 integrity/index failure; 5 Android operation failure;
130 interrupted. Network or filesystem exceptions may return 1.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apkg (1),
.BR adb (1)
